#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_exact

#% text
# `is_exact(x)` gives `true` when `x` is an exact number: an integer, a fraction, or a complex number with exact parts.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Symbols and expressions are not numbers, so they give `false` even when exact, like `pi` or `sqrt(2)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_exact(1/3)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_exact(1 + im)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_exact(0.5)
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Exact constants and expressions are not exact numbers:

#% cell
[is_exact(pi), is_exact(sqrt(2))]
#% output
#= [false, false]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_inexact`, `n`, `rationalize`
